<title>RUSSIA: Russian 161-day T-bill yields 28.31 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 161-day T-bill yields 28.31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 161-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 28.31 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in the 28.91-30.71 percent range.</p>
<p>The 22079 issue, maturing on October 22, 1997, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed on Tuesday at 88.16 to yield 29.01 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the 161-day T-bill auction:  </p>
<p>    Series number		 22082</p>
<p>    Issue volume		  4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		5.27 trln</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		   4.64 trln</p>
<p>    Sold			    3.12 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			2.78 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		 88.90 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price     88.79 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		 28.31 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield    28.62 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			   161 day</p>
<p>    Maturity date		 Oct 15, 1997</p>
<p>On May 7 the Finance Ministry raised 5.22 trillion roubles from selling a 346-day T-bill issue, taking total proceeds from today's auctions to eight trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It has also repayed about 7.25 trillion roubles in maturing 140-day T-bills (series 22063) and paid 468.64 billion roubles in interest on series 24006 OFZ interest-bearing bond.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
